   - Strings representing numbers in decimal, hexadecimal (e.g., "0x2A"), octal (e.g., "052"), or binary (e.g., "0b101010") formats.
4. Check if the parsed integer is one of the allowed values: {0, 1, 2, 3, 10, 11, 42}.

